<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Database Basics</title>

    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background: #eefbf7;
            padding: 30px;
        }

        .container {
            max-width: 850px;
            margin: auto;
            background: white;
            padding: 30px;
            border-radius: 18px;
        }

        h1 {
            text-align: center;
            color: #147d61;
        }

        .topic {
            background: #e6f8f1;
            padding: 18px;
            margin: 15px 0;
            border-radius: 12px;
        }

        h2 {
            color: #147d61;
        }

        code {
            background: white;
            padding: 5px 8px;
            border-radius: 5px;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

<div class="container">

    <h1>🗄️ Database Basics</h1>

    <div class="topic">
        <h2>What is a Database?</h2>
        <p>
            A database is an organized collection of data that can be
            stored, accessed and managed efficiently.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="topic">
        <h2>Table</h2>
        <p>
            A table stores related information using rows and columns.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="topic">
        <h2>Record</h2>
        <p>
            A record is a single row containing information about one item.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="topic">
        <h2>Field</h2>
        <p>
            A field represents a particular type of information in a table.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="topic">
        <h2>Example</h2>
        <p>
            A student database may contain fields such as
            <code>ID</code>, <code>Name</code>, <code>Course</code> and
            <code>Marks</code>.
        </p>
    </div>

</div>

</body>
</html>
